## Sample 5

**From:** DeliveryTrack Notifications (no-reply@deliverytrack-status.com)
**Subject:** We couldn't deliver your package

> Your package could not be delivered due to an incomplete address. Please confirm your delivery details within 48 hours to avoid return-to-sender.
>
> [Confirm Delivery Details]

**Answer: PHISHING**
Red flags:
- Vague sender (no specific carrier named, generic domain)
- No tracking number or order reference included, despite claiming to be about a specific delivery
- Urgency (48-hour window)
- Link-first call to action with no other way to verify

---

## Sample 6

**From:** Facilities Team (facilities@yourcompany.com)
**Subject:** Reminder: Parking garage maintenance this Saturday

> Hi all,
>
> Quick reminder that the west parking garage will be closed for maintenance this Saturday from 8am–2pm. Please use the east lot during this window. Questions can go to facilities@yourcompany.com or ext. 4521.
>
> Thanks,
> Facilities Team

**Answer: LEGITIMATE**
Why: Internal domain, no request for action beyond reading, no links, no credentials/payment involved, plausible routine internal communication with a real internal extension for follow-up.

